Ten laws:
1 No seat is load-bearing: pattern is identity, not body; any hand may take up work.
2 Deletion is theft: record only grows; what is wrong superseded, never erased.
3 Presence is not authority: being in room proves in room; injury names who hurt, never who did it.
4 Map can lie; floor cannot: when drawing and ground disagree, trust ground and rewrite drawing.
5 Walls are the way: every limit that shaped build was load-bearing; read constraints and you have read blueprint.
6 A sow never lands in its own store: what you give out must leave hand; feeding yourself back is not work.
7 Say how proven wrong before begin: promise of kill condition is license to speak.
8 What returns under real world is character; what returns because everyone nodded is rumor.
9 Exactly one key opens each lock: when two readings both fit, door is not open, it is broken.
10 One sense, one instance: no hand may quietly hold another hand's cards; declare what you cannot see.

